// The house of Vettius at Brigodunon: its man, Vellaunos's guest (Epomeduos,
// or the freedman Diodotos; see brig_house_arrive). What he asks depends on
// Act I. Routes: pay the line (or buy back the held hostages); read his paper;
// show him the door; follow him to Cabillonum (Sneak, or clumsily); kill him
// under the roof (guest-murder); let him go and wait on the road
// (enc_house_road).
=== start
[flag house_talked] -> again
~ set house_talked
[flag house_epo, flag factor_turned] -> partner
[flag house_epo] -> epo
-> dio

=== epo
Epomeduos has the guest's place by the fire, a cup of Vellaunos's beer untouched beside him and a stylus behind his ear. He gets up when you come in, which a guest doesn't have to do.

"We've met," he says. "Avaricum. You were asking about grain." The patient smile of a man paid by the line. "Today I'm here for the house of Vettius, not for Dannotalos. It's the same account. It's always the same account."
-> claim

=== partner
Epomeduos has the guest's place by the fire. When he sees you he doesn't get up, and he doesn't smile. He waits until Vellaunos has gone to see about the meat.

"Partner." He keeps his voice low. "I asked for this errand so it would be me and not somebody else. Listen to me before you listen to the house."

"Brigodunon is in the book. Not the three children: the hill. Every hearth, every head, on Dannotalos's account, to be collected after the harvest. The book is kept at Cabillonum, on the Arar, in Vettius's strongroom. I've seen the page." He turns his cup round once. "I'm supposed to sell you protection. Protection means your line is struck, for a price, for now. Pay it if you like. It won't save anyone else on the page."
~ set house_paper_read; known cabillonum; quest brig_line start; quest brig_line seat; quest house_vettius start
-> claim

=== dio
A man in a Roman tunic and a good Gallic cloak has the guest's place by the fire. He stands, bows the small exact bow of a freedman who knows what a bow is worth, and lays a sealed tablet on the bench beside him.

"Diodotos, freedman of Aulus Vettius Calvus, of Cabillonum." His Gallic is careful and correct. "Your chief has been very hospitable. I've come about the house's business with Brigodunon. It won't take long. We pay on time and we write everything down, and we expect the same of others."
-> claim

=== claim
[!quest brig_line active, !quest brig_line done] ~ quest brig_line start
[flag house_owed] -> owed
[flag house_claim_held] -> held
-> protect

=== owed
"Three persons were bought by the house from the depot at Noviodunum, paid for, and entered. They are now in Brigodunon." He doesn't look round, but he doesn't need to: through the wall you can hear Eponina laughing at something. "The house isn't unreasonable. It doesn't want them back. They'd only run again. It wants its money, and some assurance against further losses, because Brigodunon is in the book for later, the whole hill. The assurance costs {price brig_line} silver. Then the line is struck, and nobody from the house comes up this hill again."
-> hub

=== held
"Three persons from Brigodunon are at Noviodunum, bought and entered for delivery after the season's fighting." He says it gently, as if it were good news. "The house could sell them back to you, delivered after the harvest on Dannotalos's word. And Brigodunon itself is in the book for later, the whole hill. For {price brig_line} silver the house strikes the line, and nobody from the house comes up this hill again."
-> hub

=== protect
"The house has no claim on any persons from Brigodunon. The quartermaster at Noviodunum wrote yours off, and the house respects other people's books." A small dry pause. "But Brigodunon is in our book all the same, for later. The whole hill. These are uncertain times. For {price brig_line} silver the house strikes the line, and nobody from the house comes up this hill again."
-> hub

=== again
[flag house_epo] Epomeduos looks up from the fire. "Well, partner?"
[flag house_dio] Diodotos puts his cup down. "Have you decided?"
-> hub

